config PS2_SMAP
	tristate "PlayStation 2 native SMAP Ethernet"
	depends on SONY_PS2 && NETDEVICES && ETHERNET
	select PHYLIB
	select PS2_IOP_BRIDGE
	help
	  Native 10/100 Ethernet on a Sony Network Adaptor, supported PC Card
	  adapter, or a Slim console with integrated SMAP. The IOP accesses the
	  FIFOs and PHY through DEV9; Linux transfers packets over bounded SIF
	  RPCs and manages the PHY with phylib. This avoids the EE register window
	  that is unavailable on Slim hardware. The DEV9 1.2 firmware supplies
	  the factory MAC and leaves shared ATA interrupt/DMA ownership intact.
	  An Ethernet adapter is required on consoles without an integrated port.
	  A legacy direct EE backend is available for development. Physical
	  Ethernet acceptance on each supported model remains pending.
